00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:26.860
A 2020 management science paper on Estimize found at Trap and shared information.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:32.280
The more public information a user viewed before an earnings forecast, the less weight

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.220
that user put on private information.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:40.680
The individual forecast got better, the consensus got worse, because useful private information

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.940
never entered the average.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:46.940
Experiments that hid information from randomly selected users confirmed the point.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.720
More independent forecasts made a more accurate consensus.

